From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: enable USB host (OTG)

The port was limited to "peripheral", so USB-C adapters (WiFi dongles,
ethernet, keyboards) could not be used.

Switch to dr_mode = "otg" plus usb-role-switch. The role switch matters for
more than convenience: without it, dwc3_drd_init() takes the ID-pin OTG path,
which requests an "otg" interrupt. This SoC declares only a single interrupt
on the dwc3 node, so that path is at best fragile and can fail the probe,
which would take USB (and with it the only SSH access on this device) down.
dwc3_setup_role_switch() needs no extra interrupt and registers the switch
with allow_userspace_control.

role-switch-default-mode = "peripheral" keeps the port coming up as a gadget,
so USB networking and SSH keep working exactly as before. Host mode is opted
into at runtime:

	echo host   > /sys/kernel/debug/usb/4e00000.usb/mode
	echo device > /sys/kernel/debug/usb/4e00000.usb/mode

Note that dwc3_mode_write() silently discards the write when dr_mode is not
OTG (drivers/usb/dwc3/debugfs.c), which is why that debugfs file existed but
did nothing before this change.

There is no Type-C port controller driver for this device in mainline
(/sys/class/typec and /sys/class/usb_role are both empty), so role detection
is manual for now.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -566,7 +566,36 @@
 };
 
 &usb_1_dwc3 {
-	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	/*
+	 * "otg" instead of "peripheral" so the port can be used as a host
+	 * (adaptadores USB-C: WiFi, ethernet, teclados...).
+	 *
+	 * This phone has no Type-C driver in mainline (nothing under
+	 * /sys/class/typec or /sys/class/usb_role), so automatic role detection
+	 * does not work: the port comes up in device mode, which is exactly what
+	 * we want, since SSH access goes over the USB gadget.
+	 *
+	 * Switching to host is done by hand through the dwc3 debugfs:
+	 *   echo host   > /sys/kernel/debug/usb/4e00000.usb/mode
+	 *   echo device > /sys/kernel/debug/usb/4e00000.usb/mode
+	 *
+	 * Note that dwc3_mode_write() drops the write SILENTLY if dr_mode is not
+	 * OTG (drivers/usb/dwc3/debugfs.c), which is why with "peripheral" the
+	 * file exists but does nothing.
+	 */
+	dr_mode = "otg";
+
+	/*
+	 * usb-role-switch is the SAFE route: it makes dwc3 take
+	 * dwc3_setup_role_switch() instead of the ID pin OTG path, which asks for
+	 * an "otg" interrupt this SoC does not declare (the node has a single
+	 * interrupt) and could fail the probe, taking USB and SSH down with it.
+	 *
+	 * It also registers the role switch with allow_userspace_control, so a
+	 * role switch shows up under /sys/class/usb_role to change roles.
+	 */
+	usb-role-switch;
+	role-switch-default-mode = "peripheral";
 };
 
 &usb_1_hsphy {
